  s0: Release active#59; input retained
  s1: Completion receipt durable#59; inputs retained
  s2: Held#59; effects unresolved#59; input retained
  s3: Abandonment recorded without safe readback or authority
  s4: Completed input deleted#59; shared key still pinned
  s5: Held#59; worker lost#59; effects unresolved#59; input retained
  s6: Held#59; effects read back#59; explicit authority pending
  s7: Inputs tombstoned#59; key-reference proof pending
  s8: Held#59; abandonment authorized#59; receipt pending
  s9: Abandonment receipt durable#59; inputs retained
  s10: No retained key references#59; safe to retire key
  s11: Abandoned input deleted#59; shared key still pinned
  s12: No retained input references#59; key retired
  [*] --> s0
  s0 --> s1: controller records the complete release receipt
  s0 --> s2: release enters a durable hold
  s0 --> s0: another operation deletes its input with a terminal receipt
  s1 --> s4: delete this input and write its receipt-bound tombstone
  s2 --> s3: controller records the abandonment receipt
  s2 --> s5: worker lease is lost
  s2 --> s6: readback proves external effects settled
  s1 --> s7: delete this input and write its receipt-bound tombstone
  s4 --> s7: another operation deletes its input with a terminal receipt
  s5 --> s2: successor claims read-only reconciliation
  s6 --> s3: controller records the abandonment receipt
  s6 --> s8: owner signs explicit abandonment authority
  s7 --> s10: controller verifies no retained record uses this key
  s8 --> s9: controller records the abandonment receipt
  s3 --> s7: delete this input and write its receipt-bound tombstone or another operation deletes its input with a terminal receipt
  s9 --> s11: delete this input and write its receipt-bound tombstone
  s10 --> s12: retire the now-unreferenced key version
  s9 --> s7: delete this input and write its receipt-bound tombstone
  s11 --> s7: another operation deletes its input with a terminal receipt
